    <node id="Care Team">
      <data key="d0">Care Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Care Team refers to a multidisciplinary group of healthcare professionals and support personnel involved in the comprehensive management of patients with various medical conditions, particularly cancer. This team encompasses a wide range of specialists including medical oncologists, radiation oncologists, surgeons, radiologists, nurses, mental health professionals, and other support staff who collaborate to diagnose, treat, and monitor patients. Their responsibilities include staging cancer, planning treatment strategies, administering therapies such as surgery, radiation, or systemic treatments, and providing ongoing patient support. 

In addition to physical treatment, the Care Team plays a crucial role in offering emotional and psychological support, counseling, and guidance to address mental health concerns and support patient well-being throughout their treatment journey. For specific cancers such as breast cancer, lung cancer, Hodgkin lymphoma, leukemia, and skin cancer, the Care Team comprises specialized professionals with expertise in those areas to ensure tailored and effective care. 

The team is also responsible for patient communication, blood test monitoring—including laboratory results like CBC measurements—and coordinating care across different specialties. They support patients in managing symptoms, distress, and potential emergencies, emphasizing a holistic approach to healthcare that combines medical treatment with psychosocial support. Overall, the Care Team aims to provide comprehensive, coordinated, and patient-centered care, ensuring optimal health outcomes and quality of life for patients dealing with cancer and other complex medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
