    <node id="Blood Tests">
      <data key="d0">Blood Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood tests are comprehensive diagnostic procedures that analyze blood samples to detect a wide range of health conditions, abnormalities, and disease markers. They serve as essential tools in assessing overall health, identifying organ function, and monitoring disease progression or treatment responses.

Specifically, blood tests can evaluate hormone secretion levels, such as thyroid hormones and TSH, to diagnose and monitor endocrine disorders and thyroid cancers. They are also used to measure specific tumor markers relevant to various cancers, including breast, prostate, ovarian, pancreatic, and liver cancers. For example, tests like PSA are vital in prostate cancer diagnosis, while biomarkers like CEA aid in detecting and managing colorectal and other cancers. Additionally, blood tests can detect blood cell abnormalities, genetic mutations, and biomarkers associated with hematologic malignancies such as leukemia (AML, ALL, Hodgkin lymphoma, and lymphoma) and lymphoma. 

In oncology, blood tests are instrumental in establishing the extent of cancer, guiding treatment decisions, and monitoring treatment efficacy. They include complete blood counts, blood chemistry profiles, and organ function tests like liver function tests and alkaline phosphatase. These assessments are also used pre-treatment to evaluate patient health, especially before chemotherapy, radiotherapy, or surgery, and during treatment to monitor side effects and disease progression.

Moreover, blood tests evaluate specific functions such as adrenal hormone levels for adrenal tumors and assess the endocrine function during or after therapies like head and neck radiation. They also play a role in diagnosing conditions like esophageal cancer, throat cancer, and in detecting abnormal cells or genetic mutations associated with various malignancies. When combined with other diagnostic tools like imaging and biopsies, blood tests provide essential information that informs diagnosis, treatment planning, and prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
