    <node id="Mohs Surgeon">
      <data key="d0">Mohs Surgeon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Mohs surgeon is a dermatologist with advanced training who removes tumors and performs reconstruction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560447</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgical Oncologist">
      <data key="d0">Surgical Oncologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical oncologist diagnoses and surgically treats cancerous tumors, including complex cases beyond the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical oncologist performs operations to remove breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560447</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Oncologist">
      <data key="d0">Medical Oncologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical oncologist prescribes cancer-treatment drugs such as chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor who specializes in treating cancer with systemic therapies such as chemotherapy for AML.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor who treats cancer with chemotherapy and other medicines.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical oncologist treats cancer primarily using systemic drug therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical oncologist treats cancer using systemic therapies like chemotherapy, hormonal therapy, and targeted therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical oncologist is a healthcare specialist involved in the management and treatment of thyroid cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical oncologist treats cancer using systemic therapies such as chemotherapy and immunotherapy and coordinates cancer patient care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560447</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bone Marrow Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Bone Marrow Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A Bone Marrow Biopsy is a medical procedure used to obtain a small sample of bone and marrow tissue, typically from the pelvis, for diagnostic examination. This procedure involves the insertion of a needle—often a wider needle—to extract a core sample of marrow tissue, usually performed after local anesthesia and sedation to ensure patient comfort. The tissue sample collected can be examined for various purposes, including testing biomarkers, genetic alterations, and cellular morphology, which are essential for diagnosing a range of conditions such as acute myeloid leukemia (AML) and lymphoma involving bones.

The procedure is frequently conducted at the bedside and aims to provide critical information about the cellular composition and abnormalities within the bone marrow. By analyzing the retrieved tissue, clinicians can confirm diagnoses, assess disease progression, and plan appropriate treatments. In summary, a Bone Marrow Biopsy is a minimally invasive yet essential diagnostic tool for evaluating bone marrow-related diseases and conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560448</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Plastic Surgeon">
      <data key="d0">Plastic Surgeon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A plastic surgeon removes cancer and performs reconstructive procedures to restore body parts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
