    <node id="Paclitaxel">
      <data key="d0">Paclitaxel</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Paclitaxel is a chemotherapy drug used in treatment regimens for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Paclitaxel is a taxane used in chemotherapy, often combined with carboplatin, to treat ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Paclitaxel is a chemotherapy medication used in combination regimens for metastatic cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemotherapy drug often combined with carboplatin or used in other regimens for metastatic anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560482</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Ovarian Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ovarian cancer is a malignant disease characterized by the abnormal growth of malignant cells within the ovarian tissues. This disease can originate from the ovarian epithelium or supporting tissues, leading to the formation of malignant tumors in the ovaries. The development of ovarian cancer often presents with symptoms such as bloating, pelvic or abdominal pain, difficulty eating, and feeling full quickly, especially as the tumors enlarge or spread. 

The progression of ovarian cancer can involve spreading within the abdomen, with metastasis detectable through imaging modalities such as PET scans. The staging of ovarian cancer ranges from Stage I to Stage IV, reflecting the extent of tumor spread and metastasis, which guides treatment decisions. 

The disease may be associated with genetic mutations, notably in the BRCA genes and other hereditary cancer-related genes, which can influence both risk and treatment approaches. Treatments for ovarian cancer typically include surgery to remove tumors and affected tissues, chemotherapy, and other targeted therapies. In some cases, maintenance therapy is used to prevent recurrence, and ongoing surveillance is necessary to monitor for potential metastasis or disease progression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560482</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carboplatin">
      <data key="d0">Carboplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Carboplatin is a platinum chemotherapy drug used for treating squamous cell skin cancer among others.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboplatin is a chemotherapy drug often combined with Paclitaxel for ovarian cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboplatin is an alternative platinum chemotherapy drug used if cisplatin is not tolerated or suitable.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used as part of treatment regimens, especially for PD-L1–positive cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;A platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in regimens for treating metastatic anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A platinum-based chemotherapy medication that can damage the kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560482</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oxaliplatin">
      <data key="d0">Oxaliplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Oxaliplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in ovarian cancer therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemotherapy drug included in regimens with “OX,” known to cause nerve damage (neuropathy).&lt;SEP&gt;A platinum-based chemotherapy medication used in combination in treatment regimens for metastatic anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A platinum-based chemotherapy medication that can cause nerve damage in fingers and toes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560483</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1A Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1A Ovarian Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1A ovarian cancer is confined to one ovary with an intact capsule and no external invasion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
