    <node id="Stage 1C2">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1C2</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1C2 involves ovarian cancer with capsule rupture before surgery or surface involvement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560483</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1C3">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1C3</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1C3 involves ovarian cancer with cancer cells found in ascites or washings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560483</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chemotherapy Regimen">
      <data key="d0">Chemotherapy Regimen</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific combination or sequence of chemotherapeutic drugs used to treat AML.&lt;SEP&gt;The preferred chemotherapy regimen for ovarian cancer involves paclitaxel with carboplatin every 3 weeks for six cycles.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific plan combining various chemotherapy drugs used to treat AML, often tailored to patient needs and disease characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560483</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancers">
      <data key="d0">Cancers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancers refer to malignant growths, with ovarian cancers having stages from I to IV to describe progression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ascites">
      <data key="d0">Ascites</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Fluid accumulation in the abdominal cavity, which can be a sign of advanced ovarian cancer spread.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascites is the abnormal buildup of fluid in the abdomen, which can contain cancer cells in ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Washings">
      <data key="d0">Washings</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Washings refer to the fluid sample collected during surgery or diagnostic procedures to detect cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distant Lymph Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Distant Lymph Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Distant lymph nodes are lymphatic tissues located away from the primary tumor site, involved in Stage 4B spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spleen">
      <data key="d0">Spleen</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The spleen is the largest lymphatic organ, making lymphocytes and playing a key role in blood filtration and storage.&lt;SEP&gt;The spleen is an organ involved in immune response, which can be affected in advanced ovarian cancer (Stage 4B).&lt;SEP&gt;The spleen is an organ involved in immune response and blood filtration, often affected in SLL.&lt;SEP&gt;A lymphatic organ involved in blood filtering, often enlarged in blood cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Malignant Pleural Effusion">
      <data key="d0">Malignant Pleural Effusion</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Malignant pleural effusion refers to cancer cells present in the fluid around the lungs, characteristic of Stage 4A.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Peritoneal Cavity">
      <data key="d0">Peritoneal Cavity</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The peritoneal cavity is the abdominal space that may contain spread of ovarian cancer, especially in stages 3 and 4.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Peripheral Neuropathy">
      <data key="d0">Peripheral Neuropathy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Peripheral neuropathy is a common side effect of paclitaxel, causing pain, tingling, and numbness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ovarian Surface">
      <data key="d0">Ovarian Surface</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The outer surface of the ovary can be involved in certain stages, such as Stage 1C3 with surface cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ocellular Carcinoma (HCC)">
      <data key="d0">Ocellular Carcinoma (HCC)</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Ocellular carcinoma (HCC) is a primary form of liver cancer and the focus of the discussed book.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Factor">
      <data key="d0">Risk Factor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A characteristic or exposure increasing the likelihood of developing lung cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk factors are elements that increase the likelihood of developing liver cancer, including liver disease conditions such as cirrhosis or chronic hepatitis B.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk factors are elements that increase the likelihood of developing bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Screening">
      <data key="d0">Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Screening involves tests like mammograms aimed at early detection of breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening encompasses tests such as ctDNA, imaging, and blood tests used to detect and monitor colon cancer and other health conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing procedures like cervical biopsy, health history, physical exam, blood tests, and imaging to diagnose and stage cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening involves regular tests performed to detect disease presence in asymptomatic individuals, aiding early diagnosis of liver cancer if at risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560484</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chronic Hepatitis B">
      <data key="d0">Chronic Hepatitis B</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic hepatitis B is a long-term viral infection that increases the risk of liver cancer and is a key risk factor discussed in the context of liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560485</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Liver Cancer Screening Program">
      <data key="d0">Liver Cancer Screening Program</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A health initiative providing regular screening for individuals with liver disease to detect cancer early.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560485</data>
      <data key="d6" />
