    <node id="Patient">
      <data key="d0">Patient</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A patient is an individual who seeks and receives medical care for various health-related concerns, diagnoses, or conditions. Patients are encouraged to actively participate in their healthcare by asking questions, sharing concerns, and engaging in detailed discussions with healthcare providers. This active involvement extends to planning treatments, discussing results, and making informed decisions about their care, including aspects like pregnancy planning or lifestyle modifications such as exercise and diet.

Specifically, patients with certain conditions, such as chronic myeloid leukemia (CML), are advised to seek care at specialized centers and to take an active role in treatment planning to optimize outcomes. Similarly, patients undergoing screening, diagnosis, or treatment for cancers like prostate, liver, or inflammatory breast cancer are involved in providing health histories, experiencing symptoms, and consenting to procedures. For example, a patient diagnosed with inflammatory breast cancer may experience symptoms such as skin changes and pain, which lead to diagnosis, while others might undergo imaging tests to monitor or diagnose their health conditions.

Overall, patients encompass a broad spectrum of individuals engaged in managing health concerns, from routine screenings and diagnostic procedures to complex treatments, emphasizing the importance of active participation and communication in the healthcare process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560489</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Test Results">
      <data key="d0">Test Results</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Test results refer to the findings obtained from a variety of diagnostic procedures such as blood tests, biopsies, imaging studies, genetic testing, and biomarker assessments. These results are fundamental in establishing accurate diagnoses, characterizing disease features, and guiding treatment strategies across multiple medical conditions, including cancers like chronic myeloid leukemia (CML), follicular lymphoma (FL), acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), prostate cancer, breast cancer, stomach cancer, and liver cancer, as well as conditions like central B-cell lymphomas (CBCL).

In the context of cancer diagnosis and management, test results commonly include parameters such as tumor stage, grade groups, receptor status, genetic alterations, and biomarker levels. For example, PSA levels, tumor staging (TNM), and biopsy findings play critical roles in assessing prostate cancer risk, cancer staging, and the extent of disease. Genetic and biomarker information gathered from blood, tissue, and genetic testing further aid in personalized treatment planning and monitoring. Imaging studies contribute valuable visual insights into disease location, receptor expression, and disease extent, which are essential for formulating appropriate treatment strategies.

Overall, test results serve as vital clinical reports that integrate data from various diagnostic modalities. They enable clinicians to determine the presence, type, extent, and specific features of diseases, thereby informing prognosis and tailored therapies. The comprehensive analysis of these results is indispensable across a wide spectrum of medical conditions, ensuring accurate diagnosis and optimized patient care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560489</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
