    <node id="Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgery, as a comprehensive medical treatment, primarily involves the physical removal of cancerous tissues to achieve cure or manage the disease. It is the most common and often primary treatment approach for a wide variety of cancers, including skin cancers such as basal cell carcinoma, lung cancer, ovarian cancer, prostate cancer, thyroid cancer, colon cancer, cervical cancer, gliomas, bladder cancer, and other malignant tumors. In the case of skin cancer, surgery typically entails excising the cancerous tissue, sometimes requiring procedures like lymph node removal to ensure comprehensive treatment.

For cancers such as ovarian, prostate, thyroid, and cervical cancer, surgery involves removing the affected organs or tissues, including the ovaries, fallopian tubes, uterus, prostate gland, or thyroid gland, respectively. Procedures may also include the removal of nearby tissues, lymph nodes, or parts of organs like the omentum or bladder, especially in advanced cases. Based on the cancer stage and invasion level, surgery may range from removing a portion of an organ (partial resection) to complete excision (e.g., hysterectomy, mastectomy, or radical resection). In certain cases, surgery is used for pathological staging, providing important diagnostic information.

In addition to organ removal, surgical interventions for cancer often encompass specialized procedures such as pelvic exenteration, radical hysterectomy, or tumor resections designed to excise invasive or larger tumor masses. For brain cancers like gliomas, surgery involves removing tumor tissue with careful attention to preserve vital brain functions, sometimes leaving residual cells to minimize damage. In bladder cancer, surgery may include removing tumors completely or performing cystectomy to remove the entire bladder, depending on the extent of disease.

Overall, surgery is a versatile and essential treatment modality in oncology, employed not only for curative intent but also to reduce tumor burden, facilitate staging, or alleviate symptoms. Its application varies depending on the type, location, stage of the cancer, and patient health, making it a cornerstone of cancer management across numerous medical disciplines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
