    <node id="Metabolic Panel">
      <data key="d0">Metabolic Panel</data>
      <data key="d1">test</data>
      <data key="d2">A blood test to assess kidney, liver function, and overall metabolic health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560526</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Beta-2 Microglobulin">
      <data key="d0">Beta-2 Microglobulin</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A blood marker that can be elevated in lymphoid cancers like CLL and used for prognosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-2 microglobulin is a small protein found on cells, elevated levels of which may indicate CLL progression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560526</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FISH">
      <data key="d0">FISH</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) uses probes to identify specific DNA sequences and abnormalities at a small scale, often for known changes.&lt;SEP&gt;FISH is used to detect specific DNA abnormalities in leukemia cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) uses probes to detect specific DNA sequences in cells for genetic analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A genetic test that detects chromosomal abnormalities associated with blood cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560526</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DNA Sequencing">
      <data key="d0">DNA Sequencing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A technique to analyze genetic mutations in blood cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA sequencing is a technique used to find mutations in specific genes like TP53 and IGHV, which influence CLL treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560526</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CpG-Stimulated Karyotype">
      <data key="d0">CpG-Stimulated Karyotype</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic analysis method used to identify chromosomal abnormalities in blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560526</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clinical Trials">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Trials</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Clinical Trials are systematic research studies designed to evaluate the safety and effectiveness of new and existing medical treatments, interventions, drugs, or devices. These studies play a crucial role in advancing medical knowledge by testing innovative therapies across various conditions, especially cancer. For instance, clinical trials are employed to assess new treatments for cancers such as acute myeloid leukemia (AML), cervical cancer, thyroid cancer, gliomas, and bladder cancer, among others.

Typically, clinical trials for cancer treatment are conducted in phases, numbered from 1 to 4, to thoroughly establish the safety, optimal dosages, and efficacy of new therapies. Participation in clinical trials often provides patients with access to investigational treatments that are not yet widely available, offering potential benefits and contributing to the development of new treatment options. These studies are essential for translating scientific discoveries into clinical practice, helping bring innovative solutions to patients in need.

In addition to testing new treatments, clinical trials may also explore alternative approaches or combinations of therapies, with a focus on targeted therapies based on biomarker findings—particularly in conditions like gliomas. Overall, clinical trials are fundamental to medical research, enabling the progression from laboratory discoveries to real-world medical applications, ultimately enhancing patient care and expanding therapeutic options across various medical fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560527</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LDH">
      <data key="d0">LDH</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) levels may be increased in specific ovarian cancers and aid diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) is an enzyme that can be elevated in blood cancers and indicates tissue damage or disease activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560527</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunoglobulins">
      <data key="d0">Immunoglobulins</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunoglobulins are antibodies produced by immune cells, and their abnormal levels can be indicative of blood cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560527</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reticulocyte Count">
      <data key="d0">Reticulocyte Count</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A blood test that measures immature red blood cells, indicating bone marrow activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560527</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Haptoglobin">
      <data key="d0">Haptoglobin</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A protein that binds free hemoglobin; levels can change in hemolytic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560527</data>
