      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Epithelium">
      <data key="d0">Epithelium</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The epithelium is the innermost lining of the esophagus, made of squamous cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The epithelium is the outermost layer of the oral mucosa composed of stratified squamous cells, which may be keratinized or nonkeratinized depending on the region.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560530</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mouth Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Mouth Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mouth cancer, also called oral cavity cancer, develops in parts of the mouth such as lips, gums, lining inside cheeks and lips, tongue, palate, alveolar ridge, floor of the mouth, and retromolar trigone. It is primarily a type of head and neck cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth cancer refers to cancer that develops in parts of the mouth, including the lips, tongue, gums, and other oral cavity areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth cancer is a malignancy occurring in the tissues of the mouth, including tongue, gums, and other oral structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer occurring in the mouth (oral cavity), referenced as part of head and neck cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560531</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oral Cavity">
      <data key="d0">Oral Cavity</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The oral cavity includes parts such as the lips, cheeks, tongue, gums, floor of the mouth, palate, and retromolar trigone where mouth cancer can develop.&lt;SEP&gt;The oral cavity is the space inside the mouth, including the lips, gums, cheeks, tongue, palate, and floor, serving functions such as breathing, talking, eating, and swallowing.&lt;SEP&gt;The oral cavity includes the mouth, teeth, and throat, which can be examined visually or via special tools like fiberoptic scopes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560532</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bony Ridges">
      <data key="d0">Bony Ridges</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The bony ridges in the mouth include the alveolar ridge, which holds the teeth sockets and supports dental structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560532</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="White Blood Cells">
      <data key="d0">White Blood Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">White blood cells (leukocytes) are immune cells that fight infections and include granulocytes, monocytes, and lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cells are immune cells in blood, whose abnormal forms characterize AML.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cells are immune system cells that can be analyzed using blood tests and flow cytometry to detect differences and presence of biomarkers.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cells are immune cells including lymphocytes, granulocytes, and monocytes involved in infection fight and immune response.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cells are immune system cells, and their counts are measured in a differential to assess health status and detect conditions like leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cells (WBCs) fight infections and include granulocytes, monocytes, and lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cells are immune cells in the blood that help fight infections; their counts are measured in blood tests to evaluate health conditions like CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560532</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Counts">
      <data key="d0">Blood Counts</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood counts include measurements of various blood cells such as white blood cells, red blood cells, and platelets, used for diagnosing and monitoring diseases like CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH)">
      <data key="d0">Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">FISH is a lab technique used to detect genetic abnormalities in chromosomes, such as deletions or extra copies associated with CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Karyotype">
      <data key="d0">Karyotype</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A karyotype is a test that creates a picture of chromosomes to find abnormalities like missing or extra chromosome parts.&lt;SEP&gt;A karyotype is a test used to examine chromosomes for abnormalities such as extra, missing, or rearranged pieces.&lt;SEP&gt;A karyotype is a test that examines chromosomes for defects; a complex karyotype involves multiple genetic changes and impacts prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Computed Tomography">
      <data key="d0">Computed Tomography</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A diagnostic imaging procedure that uses multiple X-ray images and a computer to generate detailed cross-sectional images of body structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A CT scan uses multiple X-ray images to produce detailed 3D images to detect cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A CT scan produces detailed 3-D images of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis, potentially with contrast enhancement.&lt;SEP&gt;CT is an imaging technique used to evaluate body tissues, lymph nodes, and tumor extent in CLL diagnosis and staging.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed tomography (CT) uses X-rays and contrast to produce detailed cross-sectional images of internal body areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast Agent">
      <data key="d0">Contrast Agent</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrast may or may not be used during MRI to improve imaging details.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance injected into the bloodstream during MRI to enhance visibility of blood vessels, organs, and tissues in images.&lt;SEP&gt;Gadolinium is a contrast agent used in MRI scans to highlight areas in the brain associated with primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;A contrast agent is used during MRI to enhance picture clarity, similar to its use in CT scans.&lt;SEP&gt;A contrast agent is a chemical injected to improve the clarity of imaging results in tests like CT scans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Richter Transformation">
      <data key="d0">Richter Transformation</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Richter transformation is a medical condition described in Chapter 5 that involves a change in disease state requiring patient reading and understanding of the specific chapter.&lt;SEP&gt;Richter transformation describes the process where CLL transforms into a more aggressive lymphoma, explained in a specific chapter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cutaneous B-cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Cutaneous B-cell Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">cancer</data>
      <data key="d2">CBCL is a type of lymphoma that starts in B cells within the skin, part of the lymphatic system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560533</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cutaneous B-cell lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Cutaneous B-cell lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">cancer</data>
      <data key="d2">CBCL is a type of lymphoma that originates in B cells within the skin, part of the lymphatic system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560534</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary Cutaneous Lymphomas">
      <data key="d0">Primary Cutaneous Lymphomas</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary cutaneous lymphomas are rare lymphomas originating from abnormal B or T lymphocytes in the skin, not classified as skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560534</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cutaneous B-Cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Cutaneous B-Cell Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">CBCL develops from abnormal B cells producing antibodies, appearing as nodules under the skin similar to pimples, and includes types such as PCMZL, PCFCL, and PC-DLBCL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560534</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">CTCL develops from abnormal T cells and includes variants like mycosis fungoides, Sézary syndrome, and PCLPDs, affecting the skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560534</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphoma is a cancer of the lymph nodes that can weaken the immune system and increase skin cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoma is an abnormal overgrowth of lymphocytes, which are white blood cells that fight infections, and can occur in the central nervous system.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoma is a cancer resulting from the abnormal growth of lymphocytes, which are immune system cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoma is a type of cancer involving lymphocytes that may form multiple or a single tumors in the body, including the central nervous system.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoma is a cancer of lymphocytes originating in the lymphatic system; types include non-Hodgkin lymphoma and primary cutaneous lymphomas.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoma affects lymphocytes when they grow uncontrollably without regulation, leading to abnormal proliferation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560534</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymph Vessels">
      <data key="d0">Lymph Vessels</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymph vessels are part of the lymphatic system that drains lymph fluid from breast tissue into lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph vessels carry lymph away from breast tissue toward lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph vessels in the skin of the breast can be blocked by cancer cells in IBC, leading to characteristic symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Vessels that drain lymph fluid from the breast into lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph vessels are thin tubes that carry lymphatic fluid and lymphocytes throughout the body, essential for immune function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560534</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="B Cells">
      <data key="d0">B Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">B cells produce antibodies that help attack invading pathogens and are involved in CBCL development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T Cells">
      <data key="d0">T Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">T cells help kill tumor cells and regulate immune responses, involved in CTCL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NK Cells">
      <data key="d0">NK Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural killer cells contain granules with enzymes capable of killing tumor cells or infected cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphoid Tissue">
      <data key="d0">Lymphoid Tissue</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphoid tissue includes lymph vessels, lymph nodes, tonsils, thymus, spleen, and bone marrow involved in immune responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphatic Vessels">
      <data key="d0">Lymphatic Vessels</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphatic vessels are ducts that transport lymph throughout the body, functioning similar to blood vessels but for lymph.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphatic vessels are channels that transport lymph, a fluid involved in immune response and cancer metastasis, throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphatic vessels transport cancer cells from the tumor to nearby lymph nodes, facilitating metastasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphatic vessels are thin tubes that carry lymph and lymphocytes throughout the body, playing a vital role in immune function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Killer (NK) Cells">
      <data key="d0">Natural Killer (NK) Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">NK cells contain granules with enzymes capable of killing tumor or virus-infected cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood and Tissue Tests">
      <data key="d0">Blood and Tissue Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood and tissue tests are diagnostic procedures used to analyze blood samples and tissue specimens to identify diseases such as cutaneous B-cell lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Imaging Studies">
      <data key="d0">Imaging Studies</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Imaging studies are diagnostic tools such as X-rays, scans, or MRIs that produce visual representations of the interior of the body to help diagnose and plan treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging scans help locate enlarged lymph nodes, spleen, and other affected sites in FL.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging studies produce internal pictures of the body to help diagnose and plan treatment for throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Tests like MRI, CT, or PET used to guide AML treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging studies are diagnostic tools that help visualize internal structures and support assessment of leukemia involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging studies are diagnostic techniques such as X-rays, CT scans, or MRIs used to visualize internal structures and aid in disease diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging studies, including CT, MRI, X-rays, and ultrasounds, are used to visualize internal structures and assess the extent of diseases such as cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Head and Neck Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Head and Neck Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Head and neck cancer is a collective term for a group of malignancies that originate in various structures within the head and neck region. These cancers include those arising in the oral cavity, oropharynx, nasal cavity, nasopharynx, larynx, hypopharynx, and other related areas. The disease can affect multiple tissues such as the mouth, throat, jaw, teeth, gums, and associated structures, often impacting critical functions like speech, swallowing, and breathing.

Historically and clinically, head and neck cancers are associated with risk factors such as tobacco use, including smoking and vaping, as well as alcohol consumption. These factors contribute significantly to the development of these malignancies. The condition influences health care strategies and treatment approaches, requiring specialized management tailored to the specific location and extent of the cancer. For example, cancers like throat (oropharyngeal) cancer not only affect surrounding tissues but also have implications for dental health and structural integrity of the jaw and teeth.

Overall, head and neck cancer encompasses a diverse group of malignancies that affect a variety of tissues within the head and neck areas, with their diagnosis, prognosis, and treatment influenced by their specific site of origin and associated risk factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d0">Lymphocytes</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphocytes are a specialized type of white blood cell that play a central role in the immune system's defense mechanisms. They predominantly constitute the tissues and organs of the lymphatic system and are essential for recognizing and fighting infections. The primary subtypes of lymphocytes include B cells, T cells, and natural killer (NK) cells, each contributing uniquely to immune responses. B cells are involved in antibody production, T cells regulate immune reactions and attack infected or malignant cells, while NK cells provide rapid responses against tumor cells and virally infected cells.

Lymphocytes develop from lymphoid progenitor cells and are involved in crucial functions such as immune surveillance and pathogen elimination. Their activity is vital for maintaining immune homeostasis, but abnormalities in their development or proliferation can lead to various blood cancers. For instance, uncontrolled growth of lymphocytes can result in lymphoma, a type of cancer originating from lymphoid tissue, or leukemia, where abnormal lymphocytes multiply excessively in the bloodstream or bone marrow. Conditions like Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) and Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL) specifically involve malignant transformations of lymphocytes.

In addition to their protective roles, lymphocytes are associated with the development of certain diseases and are key indicators in diagnosing specific conditions. For example, lymphomas such as primary cutaneous B-cell lymphoma (CBCL) originate from lymphocytes, and their identification often relies on lymphocyte-related markers. Conversely, abnormal lymphocyte proliferation can also be a hallmark of hematologic cancers, emphasizing their dual role in immune defense and disease pathology. Thus, lymphocytes are fundamental components of immune function and disease processes within the lymphatic and hematologic systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Patient Portals">
      <data key="d0">Patient Portals</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Online patient portals are digital platforms that allow patients to access test results and communicate with healthcare providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
