    <node id="Tests">
      <data key="d0">Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Various diagnostic tests such as blood tests, biopsies, and genetic testing are used to diagnose and plan treatment for CML.&lt;SEP&gt;Various medical examinations and scans-including blood tests, digital rectal exams, imaging, and genetic tests-used to detect prostate cancer, determine its spread, and monitor treatment effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Tests for diagnosing primary CNS lymphoma include neurological exams, imaging (MRI or CT scan), biopsies, blood tests, and eye exams.&lt;SEP&gt;Various medical tests such as blood and urine tests, cystoscopy, biopsy, and imaging used for diagnosing and monitoring bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Tests such as blood, urine, cystoscopy, biopsy, and imaging used to diagnose, stage, and monitor bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560549</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Stem Cells">
      <data key="d0">Blood Stem Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">cell</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood stem cells, also known as hematopoietic stem cells, are a type of early progenitor cells located within the bone marrow that serve as the foundational source for all blood cell types. They are capable of differentiating into a wide range of blood components, including red blood cells, white blood cells (such as lymphocytes and myeloid cells), and platelets. These undifferentiated cells are essential for maintaining and regenerating the blood system throughout an individual's life, ensuring the continuous supply of vital blood components necessary for oxygen transport, immune defense, and clotting.

In addition to their fundamental role in normal blood formation, blood stem cells are implicated in various pathological processes. Notably, they are identified as the origin of myeloid progenitor cells, which are involved in the development of certain blood disorders such as chronic myeloid leukemia (CML). The abnormal proliferation of blood stem cells can lead to such malignancies, highlighting their significance not only in healthy physiology but also in disease contexts. Furthermore, blood stem cells are utilized in medical procedures like stem cell rescue therapies, where they are transplanted to regenerate healthy blood systems following treatments like chemotherapy or radiation.

Overall, blood stem cells are vital, multipotent early cells within the bone marrow that sustain hematopoiesis, contribute to disease processes such as leukemia, and serve as a foundation for regenerative medicine approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560550</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cystoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Cystoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Cystoscopy is a medical procedure designed to examine the interior of the bladder and urethra using an endoscopic instrument called a cystoscope. This diagnostic and investigative procedure involves inserting the cystoscope through the urethra, allowing direct visualization of the bladder lining, urethral passage, and surrounding areas. It is typically performed under anesthesia to ensure patient comfort. 

The procedure serves multiple purposes, including diagnosing urinary tract issues, detecting bladder cancers, identifying sources of bleeding, and evaluating symptoms such as hematuria or urinary difficulties. Cystoscopy enables physicians to observe abnormal tissue, tumors, or inflammatory changes within the bladder. In addition to visual assessment, the procedure often allows for tissue sampling or biopsy, enabling further pathological examination. 

In some cases, contrast agents may be injected to enhance imaging and aid in the detection of abnormalities. Beyond diagnosis, cystoscopy can also be used for therapeutic interventions, such as removing tumors, bladder stones, or other obstructions. Overall, cystoscopy is a critical tool in urology, providing a minimally invasive means to investigate and manage bladder and urethral conditions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560551</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
