    <node id="Treatment Team">
      <data key="d0">Treatment Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Treatment Team is a multidisciplinary group of healthcare professionals involved in the diagnosis, planning, administration, and management of cancer treatment. Its composition varies depending on the type of cancer but commonly includes specialists such as oncologists (medical, radiation, and surgical), gynecologic oncologists, surgeons, radiologists, nuclear medicine physicians, endocrinologists, primary care physicians, nurses, and social workers. 

The treatment team plays a critical role in evaluating patient eligibility for various treatments and clinical trials, reviewing protocols, and ensuring coordinated care. They monitor and manage the patient’s overall treatment process, including addressing side effects, guiding therapeutic decisions, and supporting patients throughout their treatment journey. In specific cases, such as ovarian, breast, bladder, and anal cancers, the team may also include geneticists, support staff, and specialists in radiology and nuclear medicine to provide comprehensive, personalized care.

Overall, the treatment team acts as an integral, collaborative unit dedicated to optimizing treatment outcomes through coordinated efforts in diagnosis, treatment planning, administration, and ongoing management of cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
