    <node id="Paraneoplastic syndromes">
      <data key="d0">Paraneoplastic syndromes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Paraneoplastic syndromes are abnormal body responses caused by lung cancer, contributing to SCLC symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560553</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chest X-ray">
      <data key="d0">Chest X-ray</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Chest X-rays are used to sometimes detect SCLC before symptoms present.&lt;SEP&gt;A chest x-ray is a quick, painless test that uses low-dose radiation to determine if cancer has spread to the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560554</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CT scans">
      <data key="d0">CT scans</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Computed tomography scans can detect SCLC before symptoms occur, although early detection is difficult.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560554</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Airways">
      <data key="d0">Airways</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Airways are pathways in the respiratory system that guide the flow of air into the lungs, including the throat, windpipe, bronchi, and bronchioli.&lt;SEP&gt;The lungs’ airways include the bronchi, bronchioli, and alveoli, where cancerous cells can grow and spread.&lt;SEP&gt;Airways in the lungs include trachea, bronchi, bronchioli, and alveoli, facilitating air passage and gas exchange.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560554</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Trachea">
      <data key="d0">Trachea</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The trachea is the windpipe that carries air into the lungs and begins the airway passages.&lt;SEP&gt;The windpipe that connects the throat to the bronchi, allowing air passage into the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;The trachea is the windpipe that splits into bronchi, guiding air into the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;The windpipe, examined during panendoscopy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560554</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bronchi">
      <data key="d0">Bronchi</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Bronchi are large airways that branch from the windpipe and divide into smaller bronchioli within the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Large passages connecting the trachea to the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Bronchi are large airways that branch from the trachea into each lung.&lt;SEP&gt;The bronchi are two main airways inside the lungs branching from the trachea.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560554</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alveoli">
      <data key="d0">Alveoli</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Alveoli are tiny sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen transfer from air to blood occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Small air sacs in the lungs where gas transfer occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Alveoli are sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen transfer to blood occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Alveoli are air sacs at the ends of bronchioli where oxygen transfer to blood occurs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560554</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lobes">
      <data key="d0">Lobes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The right lung has three lobes, and the left lung has two lobes, structures dividing the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
