    <node id="CT scan">
      <data key="d0">CT scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">CT scan is an imaging test that uses X-rays to create detailed pictures of areas inside the body, often combined with PET for cancer detection.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique that captures multiple X-rays from different angles to produce cross-sectional images of the body, used to detect cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560561</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PET/CT scan">
      <data key="d0">PET/CT scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A combined imaging technique that uses radioactive tracers and CT to identify cancer cells and their location in the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560561</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lungs">
      <data key="d0">Lungs</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The lungs are a pair of vital respiratory organs located in the chest that play a central role in the process of gas exchange. They facilitate the movement of air through airways to the alveoli, where oxygen is transferred into the blood and carbon dioxide is expelled from the bloodstream. This gas exchange capability is essential for maintaining proper respiratory function and overall metabolic homeostasis.

Additionally, the lungs serve as a site for clinical examination and assessment of health status, where anomalies such as tumors or metastases can be detected. They are prone to various pathological conditions, including the development of primary tumors and metastases from other cancers. For instance, the lungs are often affected by metastatic spread from rectal cancer, prostate cancer, and less frequently from nasopharyngeal cancer. In cases of advanced anal cancer, the lungs are recognized as a common site for metastasis. Diagnostic imaging techniques like CT scans are commonly used to evaluate lung involvement in cancer patients, revealing potential metastatic lesions and informing treatment strategies.

Overall, the lungs are essential respiratory organs with critical roles in oxygenating blood and removing carbon dioxide, while also being significant sites in the progression and diagnosis of various diseases, particularly metastatic cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urogram">
      <data key="d0">Urogram</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An imaging test using contrast dye and either CT or MRI to visualize the entire urinary tract for abnormalities or symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;A urogram is an imaging test using contrast and CT or MRI to examine the lining of the urinary tract and detect blockages or cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Ultrasound">
      <data key="d0">Renal Ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An ultrasound examining kidneys, ureters, and bladder, providing real-time, painless images.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal ultrasound is a painless, non-surgical imaging technique using real-time black and white images to visualize kidneys, ureters, and bladder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter Cystoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Chapter Cystoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A section or chapter in a medical guide explaining cystoscopy procedures and related information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pyelogram">
      <data key="d0">Pyelogram</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A pyelogram employs x-rays and contrast solution to look for blockages such as tumors, kidney stones, or blood clots in the ureters or kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biopsies">
      <data key="d0">Biopsies</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Biopsies are diagnostic procedures involving tissue sampling to confirm cancer presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies involve sampling tissue to identify the presence of disease, often used alongside other tests to inform treatment plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Secondhand Smoke">
      <data key="d0">Secondhand Smoke</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Secondhand smoke can increase the risk of bladder cancer in family and friends of smokers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Staging and Grading">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Staging and Grading</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staging and grading assess how far and how fast cancer has grown, informing prognosis and treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560562</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inherited Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Inherited Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Inherited cancer refers to cancers caused or increased by genetic mutations passed down from parents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Germline Mutations">
      <data key="d0">Germline Mutations</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Germline mutations are inherited gene mutations passed from parents to offspring, influencing hereditary cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Germline mutations are inherited genetic alterations found in every cell, increasing the risk of cancers such as bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dermis">
      <data key="d0">Dermis</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The dermis is a layer of skin located beneath the epidermis, containing connective tissue and other structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Punch Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Skin Punch Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin punch biopsy is a medical procedure that removes a small piece of skin and connective tissue using a hand-held tool for diagnostic purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a procedure where a small piece of skin and underlying tissue is removed to extract DNA unaffected by leukemia, used to identify inherited genetic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a procedure used to collect skin tissue, especially when hereditary predisposition is suspected.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a procedure to obtain skin tissue and DNA for genetic analysis to determine inherited leukemia risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Excision Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Excision Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An excision biopsy involves removing all or part of a lesion or tissue for diagnostic or treatment purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Binder">
      <data key="d0">Medical Binder</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical binder is a organized collection of medical records, test results, and important health documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical binder is a organized collection of medical records, lab tests, imaging results, and reports to assist in healthcare management and second opinions.&lt;SEP&gt;A organized record-keeping system for storing medical documents such as tests, reports, and insurance forms.&lt;SEP&gt;A folder or notebook used to organize medical records, test results, and reports for easy access and second opinions.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical binder is used to organize all medical records, including blood tests, imaging results, and reports about specific cancer types, to facilitate access and reference during appointments and second opinions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Imaging Results">
      <data key="d0">Imaging Results</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Imaging results are diagnostic reports from scans such as X-rays, CT, MRI, or PET used to visualize internal structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging results include data from scans like CT, MRI, and PET, used to evaluate internal structures and detect cancer spread.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic images from scans used to locate and evaluate tumors and other health issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic images interpreted by radiologists to identify and evaluate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast Dye">
      <data key="d0">Contrast Dye</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrast dye is a substance injected into veins to enhance imaging clarity in CT and MRI scans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560563</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Positron Emission Tomography (PET) Scan">
      <data key="d0">Positron Emission Tomography (PET) Scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A PET scan uses radioactive tracers to visualize metabolic activity and detect cancer cells inside the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma (CSCC)">
      <data key="d0">Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma (CSCC)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A common and treatable type of skin cancer predominantly caused by sun exposure, which can spread and cause serious damage if untreated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nodal Disease">
      <data key="d0">Nodal Disease</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nodal disease refers to cancer that has spread to lymph nodes, indicating regional metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Local Squamous Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Local Squamous Cell Skin Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A form of CSCC confined to the skin without lymph node involvement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Regional Squamous Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Regional Squamous Cell Skin Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A stage of CSCC where cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Actinic Keratosis">
      <data key="d0">Actinic Keratosis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A rough, scaly skin lesion with higher likelihood of transforming into squamous cell carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sunscreen">
      <data key="d0">Sunscreen</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sunscreen is a preventive measure to protect skin from sun damage, reducing skin cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Smoking Cessation Websites">
      <data key="d0">Smoking Cessation Websites</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The text provides URLs for online support for quitting tobacco, including SmokeFree.gov, BeTobaccoFree.gov, and CDC.gov/tobacco.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stages of Bladder Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stages of Bladder Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The stages (0, 1, 2, 3, 4) describe the progression and spread of bladder cancer, with subgroups indicating specific invasion levels and spread to lymph nodes and organs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 0">
      <data key="d0">Stage 0</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 0 pancreatic cancer is limited to the innermost layer of the duct wall.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 0 is noninvasive breast cancer, such as ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS).&lt;SEP&gt;Colon cancer with abnormal cells on the innermost layer, also called carcinoma in situ.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 0 represents cases with no detectable tumor but positive Epstein-Barr virus in lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 0 bladder cancer affects only the inner lining of the bladder without invasion into deeper layers, includes subgroups 0a and carcinoma in situ.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicates abnormal cells have grown on the bladder lining without invasion into deeper tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1 NSCLC is an early stage where cancer grows from the airway into lung tissue without spreading to lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1 pancreatic cancer involves tumors 4 centimeters or smaller that have not spread outside the pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer has grown into the second or third layer of the colon wall without involving lymph nodes or outside areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1 bladder cancer has invaded the connective tissue but not the muscle layer.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicates a tumor has formed and invaded the connective tissue layer of the bladder wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 2">
      <data key="d0">Stage 2</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 2 NSCLC is considered locally advanced, often involving nearby structures or lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2 pancreatic cancer involves tumors larger than 4 centimeters or spread to 1 to 3 nearby lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer has penetrated into or beyond the fourth layer of the colon wall but has not spread to lymph nodes or outside organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2 bladder cancer has grown into the muscle layer but not into surrounding fat or spread elsewhere.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 3">
      <data key="d0">Stage 3</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 3 NSCLC is also locally advanced, with potential spread to distant lymph nodes or nearby tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3 pancreatic cancer involves growth through the pancreas to nearby arteries or spread to 4 or more lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes or involves tumor deposits in the fat around the colon.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3 bladder cancer has invaded the fatty layer of the bladder wall and may have spread to nearby lymph nodes or organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer has grown into the fat layer surrounding the bladder and may involve nearby lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Cell">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Cell</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer cells are abnormal cells compared to normal cells, with variations in appearance related to cancer grade.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LG (Low Grade)">
      <data key="d0">LG (Low Grade)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indicates cancer cells are slow growing and less aggressive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HG (High Grade)">
      <data key="d0">HG (High Grade)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indicates cancer cells are fast growing and more aggressive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urothelial Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Urothelial Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of bladder cancer that originates in urothelial cells, with variations in features and subtypes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Subtypes of Urothelial Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Subtypes of Urothelial Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Various forms of urothelial cancer that resemble other cell types, including Glandular, Squamous cell, Micropapillary, Plasmacytoid, Sarcomatoid, Nested, Lymphoepithelioma-like, Microcystic and tubular.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stages 2, 3, 4">
      <data key="d0">Stages 2, 3, 4</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Muscle-invasive bladder cancers, with increasing invasion depth and possible spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Grade">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Grade</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Assessment of how abnormal the cancer cells look under a microscope, indicating growth speed.&lt;SEP&gt;An estimate of how quickly cancer is expected to grow, indicating aggressiveness, categorized as Low or High.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer grade assesses the differentiation and expected growth rate of cancer cells, influencing treatment decisions like local excision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Resection">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Resection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure called transurethral resection of bladder tumor (TURBT) to remove tumors through the urethra.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TURBT (Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor)">
      <data key="d0">TURBT (Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A minimally invasive surgical procedure for removing bladder tumors via urethra, used for diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surrounding Fat Layer">
      <data key="d0">Surrounding Fat Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The fat tissue around the bladder that can be invaded by cancer in stage 3 bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560566</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Tissue">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Tissue</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Sample of cancerous tissue used for biomarker testing, including mutation analysis for personalized treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor tissue is sampled during biopsy to assess for mutations, MSI, HER2 expression, and other diagnostic markers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Microsatellite Instability">
      <data key="d0">Microsatellite Instability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MSI is a genetic feature that indicates mismatch repair deficiency, relevant for immunotherapy considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsatellite instability is a condition of genetic hypermutability associated with certain types of ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;MSI is a biomarker that can influence immunotherapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;High microsatellite instability (MSI-H) is a biomarker indicating genetic instability often linked to Lynch syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsatellite instability (MSI-H) is a genetic biomarker indicating a defect in DNA mismatch repair, relevant in colon cancer prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mismatch Repair">
      <data key="d0">Mismatch Repair</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MMR refers to cellular mechanisms repairing DNA mismatches; deficiency can be a biomarker for certain treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Mismatch repair is a DNA repair system that, when deficient, can lead to microsatellite instability in tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;MMR status is assessed for its role in treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HER2 Expression">
      <data key="d0">HER2 Expression</data>
      <data key="d1">biomarker</data>
      <data key="d2">HER2 is a protein whose expression levels can influence treatment choices in ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;HER2 expression refers to the presence of HER2 protein on tumor cells, relevant for certain ovarian cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRAF V600E Mutation">
      <data key="d0">BRAF V600E Mutation</data>
      <data key="d1">geneticmutation</data>
      <data key="d2">BRAF V600E mutation is an activating genetic alteration relevant in specific ovarian cancer subtypes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Folate Receptor Alpha">
      <data key="d0">Folate Receptor Alpha</data>
      <data key="d1">biomarker</data>
      <data key="d2">FRα is a protein expressed in some ovarian cancers, serving as a potential therapeutic target.&lt;SEP&gt;Folate receptor alpha (FRα) expression is a feature of ovarian cancer that can influence targeted therapy options.&lt;SEP&gt;FRα is a biomarker that guides the use of targeted therapy like mirvetuximab soravtansine-gynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RET Mutations">
      <data key="d0">RET Mutations</data>
      <data key="d1">geneticmutation</data>
      <data key="d2">RET mutations are genetic alterations that can occur in tumors, influencing treatment pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;RET mutations are genetic alterations that may be involved in ovarian cancer development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560567</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NTRK Gene Fusion">
      <data key="d0">NTRK Gene Fusion</data>
      <data key="d1">geneticalteration</data>
      <data key="d2">NTRK gene fusions are genetic alterations that can be targeted in specific therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;NTRK gene fusion involves rearrangements that can be targeted in ovarian cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;NTRK gene fusion is a genetic alteration in thyroid cancer that can be targeted with specific therapies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRCA Genes">
      <data key="d0">BRCA Genes</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">BRCA genes are involved in hereditary cancer risk, and mutations in these genes can be determined through testing to guide treatment decisions in ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;BRCA gene mutations are hereditary genetic variations that increase the risk of ovarian and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;BRCA genes are DNA sequences involved in DNA repair; mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2 increase risks of multiple cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fertility-Sparing Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Fertility-Sparing Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility-sparing surgery involves removing cancer-affected tissues while preserving the uterus to enable future pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility-sparing surgery preserves reproductive organs while treating cancer, suitable for select early-stage cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hysterectomy">
      <data key="d0">Hysterectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Hysterectomy is surgery to remove the uterus, often performed for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical removal of the uterus, including different types like extrafascial, modified radical, and radical.&lt;SEP&gt;Hysterectomy is a surgical removal of the uterus, and considerations regarding whether to preserve ovaries can influence treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure that removes the uterus and possibly surrounding tissues, affecting fertility and causing menopause.&lt;SEP&gt;Hysterectomy is a surgical removal of the uterus, typically used in treating cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of the uterus, often affecting brachytherapy placement approaches in cervical cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bilateral Salpingo-Oophorectomy">
      <data key="d0">Bilateral Salpingo-Oophorectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy (BSO) involves removing both ovaries and fallopian tubes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Salpingectomy">
      <data key="d0">Salpingectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Salpingectomy involves removing one or both fallopian tubes, which may be performed to manage early ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgical Staging">
      <data key="d0">Surgical Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgical staging assesses the extent of ovarian cancer spread by sampling tissues and lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical staging involves surgically removing and examining lymph nodes to determine the extent of cancer spread, particularly in locally advanced cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560568</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Debulking Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Debulking Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Debulking or cytoreductive surgery aims to remove as much tumor as possible, especially when cancer has spread outside the ovaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Omentum">
      <data key="d0">Omentum</data>
      <data key="d1">anatomical</data>
      <data key="d2">The omentum is a fatty tissue covering abdominal organs, often sampled or removed during surgical staging.&lt;SEP&gt;The omentum is the fatty tissue layer covering organs in the abdomen, which may be removed during surgery to check for cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Laparotomy">
      <data key="d0">Laparotomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Laparotomy is a surgical procedure involving a large abdominal incision to access and operate on ovarian tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Open surgical approach through a large abdominal incision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Laparoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Laparoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Laparoscopy is a minimally invasive surgical approach using small incisions and a camera, suitable in select cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hormone Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Hormone Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Hormone treatment may be used in some cases of ovarian cancer, especially in hormone receptor-positive tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DNA Repair">
      <data key="d0">DNA Repair</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">DNA repair is a biological process involved in correcting DNA damage, relevant for understanding mutations in ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA repair involves cellular mechanisms to correct genetic damage; mutations in repair genes like ATM, CHEK2, MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, PALB2, PMS2 can lead to increased cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="In Vitro Fertilization">
      <data key="d0">In Vitro Fertilization</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">In vitro fertilization (IVF) is assisted reproductive technology used when pregnancy isn't possible after BSO.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ureter">
      <data key="d0">Ureter</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The ureter is a tube that transports urine from the renal pelvis to the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;A tube that carries urine from the kidneys to the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seminal Vesicles">
      <data key="d0">Seminal Vesicles</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Two glands located above the prostate and behind the bladder that produce part of the fluid that becomes semen.&lt;SEP&gt;Seminal vesicles are glands located above the prostate that contribute fluids to semen.&lt;SEP&gt;Seminal vesicles are two glands located above the prostate and behind the bladder, responsible for producing and storing a component of semen.&lt;SEP&gt;Glands that produce a component of semen, involved in reproductive anatomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vas Deferens">
      <data key="d0">Vas Deferens</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A tube that transports sperm from the testicles to the urethra.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TURBT">
      <data key="d0">TURBT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure that examines and removes tumors from the bladder wall through the urethra.&lt;SEP&gt;Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor (TURBT) is a surgical procedure to remove visible bladder tumors before intravesical therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cystectomy">
      <data key="d0">Cystectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure to remove the bladder, which can be partial or radical.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560569</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radical Cystectomy">
      <data key="d0">Radical Cystectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A major surgery removing the entire bladder, nearby lymph nodes, and other organs, often used for muscle-invasive bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure involving removal of the entire bladder, nearby lymph nodes, and sometimes additional organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Radical cystectomy is a surgical procedure involving removal of the bladder and nearby organs, used for muscle-invasive bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Partial Cystectomy">
      <data key="d0">Partial Cystectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgery that removes only part of the bladder, rarely used for bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urinary Diversion">
      <data key="d0">Urinary Diversion</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure to reroute urine after bladder removal, involving different types such as ileal conduit, neobladder, or Indiana pouch.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of surgical procedures that create an alternate pathway for urine to exit the body following bladder removal.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical method that reroutes urine flow using the Indiana pouch, eliminating the need for an ostomy bag.&lt;SEP&gt;Urinary diversion is a surgical technique to reroute urine exit after bladder removal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ileal Conduit">
      <data key="d0">Ileal Conduit</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A urinary diversion where a section of the small intestine is used as a conduit for urine to exit through a stoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neobladder">
      <data key="d0">Neobladder</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A urinary diversion where a segment of small intestine creates a new bladder attached to the ureters and urethra.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560570</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Continent Cutaneous Pouch (Indiana Pouch)">
      <data key="d0">Continent Cutaneous Pouch (Indiana Pouch)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A urinary diversion where part of the large and small intestines is used to create a pouch with a stoma, requiring catheterization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pain or Burning When Urinating">
      <data key="d0">Pain or Burning When Urinating</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Common symptoms associated with urinary tract infections or other bladder conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indiana University">
      <data key="d0">Indiana University</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Indiana University is an academic institution where surgeons developed the Indiana pouch procedure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indiana Pouch">
      <data key="d0">Indiana Pouch</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Indiana pouch is a urinary diversion method using a section of the small intestine connected to a stoma, developed by surgeons at Indiana University.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stoma">
      <data key="d0">Stoma</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">An opening on the abdominal surface that allows stool exit after surgery when the rectum is removed.&lt;SEP&gt;A stoma is the opening created in the abdomen during a colostomy through which stool exits the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A stoma is an opening created in the abdominal wall for urine or stool to exit the body after organ removal or diversion procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A stoma in the wall of the abdomen is created for urine drainage in urinary diversion procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Catheter">
      <data key="d0">Catheter</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical device, such as a catheter, is tailored to individual needs and treatment plans for delivering therapies or accessing the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is a thin tube that delivers chemotherapy directly into the abdominal cavity during IP chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is a thin tube inserted into a vein to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, or blood products.&lt;SEP&gt;A tube used to insert into the stoma and pouch to drain urine multiple times a day.&lt;SEP&gt;Flexible tube used to deliver medicine into the bladder during therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Valve">
      <data key="d0">Valve</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A one-way valve made from part of the intestine prevents urine from flowing out of the stoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ostomy Bag">
      <data key="d0">Ostomy Bag</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An ostomy bag is a disposable container attached outside the body to collect urine or stool expelled through a stoma.&lt;SEP&gt;An appliance that collects urine, only needed if a different diversion method is used; the Indiana pouch negates its necessity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bacillus CalmetteGuérin">
      <data key="d0">Bacillus CalmetteGuérin</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A form of intravesical therapy using a weak bacterium to stimulate immune response against bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immune System">
      <data key="d0">Immune System</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The immune system defends the body against disease; a weakened immune system increases the risk of developing cancer and its recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;Having an impaired immune system increases the risk of developing primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;The biological system triggered by intravesical BCG to attack bladder cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560571</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic therapy is a comprehensive approach to cancer treatment that involves the use of medications capable of traveling through the bloodstream to reach and affect cancer cells throughout the entire body. This form of therapy is primarily employed when localized treatments such as surgery or radiation are insufficient, impractical, or when the cancer has metastasized. It encompasses various treatment modalities including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, immunotherapy, endocrine therapy, and other systemic agents, each designed to attack cancer cells comprehensively.

Chemotherapy is a prominent example of systemic therapy, involving drugs that circulate through the bloodstream to destroy cancer cells across different body sites. Targeted therapies are specialized agents that specifically attack certain molecules or genetic changes within cancer cells, often used in advanced cases such as thyroid cancers. Immunotherapy enhances the body's immune response to recognize and combat cancer cells. Intravenous administration is a common method for delivering these treatments, ensuring widespread distribution throughout the body.

While systemic therapy is effective against various cancers, such as acute myeloid leukemia (AML), it is also applicable in specific scenarios like basal cell skin cancer, particularly when other treatment options are unsuitable. Overall, systemic therapy plays a critical role in managing advanced or metastatic cancers by providing a means to treat malignancies comprehensively beyond localized control strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560572</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maintenance Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Maintenance Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Maintenance therapy uses systemic treatment after initial successful cancer treatment to prevent recurrence or prolong remission.&lt;SEP&gt;Maintenance therapy involves ongoing treatment to prevent cancer recurrence after initial therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated intravesical BCG or chemotherapy treatments to prevent cancer recurrence after initial therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560572</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intravesical Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Intravesical Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Intravesical chemotherapy is a localized treatment that affects only the inside of the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;A drug treatment administered directly into the bladder to kill residual cancer cells and prevent recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560572</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Treatment Schedule">
      <data key="d0">Treatment Schedule</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Intravesical chemotherapy and BCG are administered in schedules such as weekly for 6 weeks, with maintenance doses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560572</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BCG Shortage">
      <data key="d0">BCG Shortage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A global shortage of BCG used in bladder cancer treatment leading to limited availability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560572</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chemotherapy Drugs">
      <data key="d0">Chemotherapy Drugs</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Chemotherapy drugs include doxorubicin, epirubicin, docetaxel, paclitaxel, capecitabine, fluorouracil, gemcitabine, and methotrexate.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy drugs are medications that damage and destroy rapidly dividing cells, used alone or with other treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Medications used to target and kill cancer cells throughout the body, administered intravenously.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560573</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intravesical BCG">
      <data key="d0">Intravesical BCG</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Contains a weak bacterium that triggers immune response to treat bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560573</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Body Image">
      <data key="d0">Body Image</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A psychological concern related to the presence of ostomy bags or surgical alterations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560573</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aesthetic Appearance">
      <data key="d0">Aesthetic Appearance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Related to body image concerns, especially with stoma location or surgical outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560573</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic chemotherapy affects the entire body and is used to treat cancer throughout the body, often administered as a part of cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560573</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dose-Dense Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Dose-Dense Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dose-dense chemotherapy is a method of administering chemotherapy by shortening the interval between doses to accelerate treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Methotrexate">
      <data key="d0">Methotrexate</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Used in AML treatment, sometimes administered intrathecally for central nervous system involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Methotrexate is an antimetabolite involved in AML treatment protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Methotrexate is a high-dose chemotherapy drug used to treat primary CNS lymphoma, which can cause damage to organs but is effective against cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Methotrexate is the primary chemotherapy drug used to treat primary CNS lymphoma by damaging and destroying rapidly dividing cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug used as part of the ddMVAC regimen for bladder cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vinblastine">
      <data key="d0">Vinblastine</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Vinblastine is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with other medicines to treat bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Doxorubicin">
      <data key="d0">Doxorubicin</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Doxorubicin is a chemotherapy drug included in the ddMVAC combination therapy for bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Platinum">
      <data key="d0">Platinum</data>
      <data key="d1">material</data>
      <data key="d2">Platinum is a metal used in chemotherapy drugs like cisplatin, which can be effective against bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Testicles">
      <data key="d0">Testicles</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The testicles, also known as testes, are vital male reproductive organs that play a central role in the male reproductive system. They are primarily responsible for producing sperm, which is essential for male fertility, and synthesizing testosterone, the principal male sex hormone that influences secondary sexual characteristics, libido, and overall reproductive health.

Testicles are susceptible to damage from cancer and its treatments, such as chemotherapy and radiotherapy, which can impair sperm production and consequently affect fertility. Surgical removal of the testicles, known as castration, is sometimes employed as a method to block testosterone production, especially in certain medical conditions like prostate cancer. Additionally, endocrine therapies may involve suppressing testosterone levels, impacting the hormonal functions of the testicles.

Furthermore, the testicles can serve as sites for diagnostic assessment of certain diseases, including lymphoma, where imaging may be utilized to check for the spread of lymphoma to this area. Overall, the testicles are essential organs involved not only in reproductive processes but also in hormonal regulation and, potentially, in disease diagnosis and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Checkpoint Inhibitors">
      <data key="d0">Checkpoint Inhibitors</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Immune checkpoint inhibitors like Pembrolizumab and Nivolumab used for immunotherapy before colectomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkpoint inhibitors are a type of immunotherapy that blocks the body's natural braking mechanisms to enhance immune response against cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pembrolizumab">
      <data key="d0">Pembrolizumab</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is a PD-1 inhibitor used for treating squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Pembrolizumab, also called Keytruda, is an immunotherapy drug that re-activates the immune system against tumor cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is an immune checkpoint inhibitor used in certain systemic therapies for cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is a checkpoint inhibitor used to treat bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;An immune checkpoint inhibitor used to treat metastatic anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nivolumab">
      <data key="d0">Nivolumab</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Nivolumab (Opdivo) is a checkpoint inhibitor used for bladder cancer immunotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;An immune checkpoint inhibitor used to treat metastatic anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Avelumab">
      <data key="d0">Avelumab</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Avelumab (Bavencio) is a checkpoint inhibitor used in bladder cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Atezolizumab">
      <data key="d0">Atezolizumab</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Atezolizumab (Tecentriq) is a checkpoint inhibitor used in bladder cancer immunotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560574</data>
