    <node id="FDA">
      <data key="d0">FDA</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The U.S. Food and Drug Administration is responsible for approving new drugs, devices, or treatment approaches after clinical trials demonstrate safety and efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is responsible for reviewing and approving new drugs, medical devices, and treatments after clinical trials demonstrate their safety and efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Food and Drug Administration, which approves new drugs, devices, or treatment approaches that show safety and effectiveness in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is responsible for approving new drugs and treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Food and Drug Administration, responsible for approving new drugs, devices, or treatments after clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
