    <node id="Placebo">
      <data key="d0">Placebo</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An inactive substance used in some clinical trials, usually combined with standard treatment rather than used alone.&lt;SEP&gt;An inactive substance used in some clinical trials; rarely used alone, usually paired with standard treatment or a new drug.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is an inert substance used as a control in clinical trials before a participant enrolls in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance with no therapeutic effect, usually used as a control in clinical trials, but almost never used alone in cancer trials.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is an inactive substance used in clinical trials to compare against the investigational treatment and is disclosed to participants before enrollment.&lt;SEP&gt;An inactive substance that may be used in comparison with active treatments during clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560578</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bladder Removal Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Bladder Removal Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgical removal of the bladder that can cause side effects such as bleeding, infection, and sexual dysfunction.</data>
