    <node id="External Beam Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">External Beam Radiation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT) is a form of radiation treatment that involves delivering high-energy radiation from outside the body to target and destroy cancer cells. The therapy employs a machine called a linear accelerator, which precisely directs radiation beams at the tumor site while sparing surrounding healthy tissues. EBRT is applicable to a variety of cancers, including breast, cervical, and thyroid cancers, as well as lymph nodes involved in cancer spread.

In practice, EBRT involves aiming external high-energy radiation waves at the affected areas, such as the breast and lymph nodes in breast cancer, or the cervix in cervical cancer. For thyroid cancer, especially aggressive or unresectable types, EBRT serves as a valuable treatment option when surgery is not feasible or insufficient. This technique ensures targeted therapy by focusing the radiation externally, thereby maximizing tumor cell destruction while minimizing damage to adjacent normal tissues. Overall, EBRT is a widely used, non-invasive cancer treatment modality utilizing external high-energy beams to effectively target and eliminate malignant cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560580</data>
