    <node id="Anal Canal">
      <data key="d0">Anal Canal</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The anal canal connects the rectum to the anal opening and is about 4 centimeters long.&lt;SEP&gt;The anal canal is the small section of bowel between the rectum and the anus where anal cancer can develop.&lt;SEP&gt;The anal canal is a part of the anatomy where anal cancer can originate, located within the pelvis.&lt;SEP&gt;Anal canal is a part of the gastrointestinal tract that is involved in the context of anal cancer and its treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560580</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Perianal Region">
      <data key="d0">Perianal Region</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The perianal region includes the anal opening and surrounding skin.&lt;SEP&gt;The perianal region includes the anal opening and surrounding skin, can be affected by precancerous lesions.&lt;SEP&gt;The perianal region includes the anal opening and the skin directly surrounding it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560580</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chemoradiation">
      <data key="d0">Chemoradiation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Chemoradiation refers to a treatment approach that combines chemotherapy and radiation therapy to combat various types of cancer. This modality is primarily used for locally advanced cancers, where concurrent administration of these therapies enhances treatment efficacy. In particular, chemoradiation is frequently employed for cervical cancer, involving the use of external beam radiation therapy alongside platinum-based chemotherapy given simultaneously, especially in higher-stage disease. It is also used as a primary treatment for anal cancer, especially when surgery is not suitable, targeting non-metastatic cases and sometimes as a subsequent line of therapy following initial chemotherapy.

The strategy often involves external beam radiation therapy combined with chemotherapy to maximize local control of the tumor. For bladder cancer, chemoradiation aims to improve outcomes by utilizing both modalities concurrently. In cases of anal cancer, it is recommended for non-metastatic tumors that are not amenable to surgical removal, serving as an effective alternative to surgery with the goal of organ preservation.

While chemoradiation is a common and effective combined modality, it is generally not administered after certain chemotherapy regimens, such as the modified DCF, indicating some treatment-specific considerations. Overall, chemoradiation represents a synergistic approach that leverages the cytotoxic effects of chemotherapy with the local control provided by radiation therapy across multiple cancer types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560581</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anal Squamous Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Anal Squamous Cell Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Anal squamous cell carcinoma is a specific form of anal cancer starting from squamous cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Anal squamous cell carcinoma is an invasive cancer diagnosed by biopsy, requiring additional testing for treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
