    <node id="HIV">
      <data key="d0">HIV</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) is a virus that damages the immune system, increasing susceptibility to cancers like CSCC.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is the virus that causes AIDS and is associated with increased risk of primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Human immunodeficiency virus, requiring testing in patients with primary CNS lymphoma due to associated treatment considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;People with HIV have an increased risk of developing anal cancer, and testing for HIV is recommended.&lt;SEP&gt;Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection is a risk factor that weakens the immune system and increases the risk of anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV infection is a risk factor for anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560583</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunosuppressant">
      <data key="d0">Immunosuppressant</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Use of anti-rejection medicines after organ transplant can weaken immunity and raise anal cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Use of immunosuppressant drugs is a risk factor for anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560583</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vulvar Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Vulvar Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulvar cancer is a cancer affecting vulvar tissue and is associated with HPV.&lt;SEP&gt;History of vulvar cancer or precancer increases risk of anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Blood Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood cancer refers to malignant blood cell proliferation, including CML.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood cancers such as lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, or multiple myeloma are associated with increased anal cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Autoimmune Disorders">
      <data key="d0">Autoimmune Disorders</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Autoimmune conditions like Crohn's disease can weaken immune response, increasing anal cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Certain autoimmune disorders are associated with a higher risk of anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anal Sex">
      <data key="d0">Anal Sex</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">History of anal sex is a behavioral risk factor for anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;History of anal sex or sexually transmitted infections are risk factors for anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sexually Transmitted Infection">
      <data key="d0">Sexually Transmitted Infection</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">History of STI is associated with increased risk of anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anal Dysplasia">
      <data key="d0">Anal Dysplasia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Anal dysplasia refers to abnormal cellular growths in or near the anus, including LSIL, HSIL, and AIN, acting as precursors to anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LSIL">
      <data key="d0">LSIL</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion, representing mild dysplasia (CIN 1).&lt;SEP&gt;Low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (LSIL) is a mild form of anal dysplasia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HSIL">
      <data key="d0">HSIL</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL) encompasses moderate or severe dysplasia (CIN 2 and 3) and is considered a pre-cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion, representing moderate or severe dysplasia (CIN 2 and 3).&lt;SEP&gt;High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL) is a more severe form of anal dysplasia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="AIN">
      <data key="d0">AIN</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Anal intraepithelial neoplasia (AIN) is a precancerous condition associated with HPV infection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560584</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HPV Vaccine">
      <data key="d0">HPV Vaccine</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A vaccine protecting against 9 strains of HPV, including the highest-risk types, available in the United States and other countries, effective primarily in younger populations.&lt;SEP&gt;Available vaccination option for adults aged 45 years and under to prevent HPV infection, especially effective in younger populations.&lt;SEP&gt;Vaccine protecting against 9 HPV strains, including high-risk types, for prevention of HPV infection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560585</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bleeding from the Anus">
      <data key="d0">Bleeding from the Anus</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Most common symptom of anal cancer, can include blood in stool, toilet paper, or water.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560585</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anal Itching">
      <data key="d0">Anal Itching</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Common symptom of anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560585</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pain or Lump in Anal Area">
      <data key="d0">Pain or Lump in Anal Area</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Symptoms that may indicate anal cancer, warranting medical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
