    <node id="Stage">
      <data key="d0">Stage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The stage of follicular lymphoma depends on cell types and proliferation, affecting treatment strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Stages in cancer describe the extent and progression of the disease, ranging from stage 0 to stage 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage indicates how far ovarian cancer has spread, with number designations I, II, III, and IV.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage is a classification that combines TNM scores to describe how much cancer is in the body and its spread.&lt;SEP&gt;The stage describes the extent of cervical cancer before treatment, guiding treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
