    <node id="Acute Myeloid Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Acute Myeloid Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">AML is a blood cancer originating in bone marrow stem cells, leading to abnormal proliferation of myeloblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;AML is a type of leukemia characterized by accumulation of immature white blood cells called myeloblasts, which impair normal blood function.&lt;SEP&gt;AML, a serious side effect of PARP inhibitors and chemotherapy, involves rapid growth of immature white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;AML is a fast-growing cancer of immature white blood cells in the bone marrow and blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is a type of blood cancer originating in the stem cells of bone marrow, characterized by abnormal myeloblasts that impair normal blood cell production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560591</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Components">
      <data key="d0">Blood Components</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood components include plasma, red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
