    </node>
    <node id="Metastatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Metastatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Metastatic cancer refers to lung cancer that has spread beyond the lung tissue to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that has spread to distant organs or parts of the body such as liver, lungs, or brain.&lt;SEP&gt;Metastatic cancer is cancer that has spread from the primary site to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has spread from its original site to other organs such as liver, lungs, or bones.&lt;SEP&gt;Metastatic thyroid cancer has spread beyond the neck to areas such as the lungs, liver, bones, brain, or spinal cord.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that has spread from its original site to other parts of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560605</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage IV Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage IV Anal Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage IV anal cancer indicates metastatic disease present at diagnosis or after initial treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560605</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stereotactic Body Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Stereotactic Body Radiation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">SBRT is a highly precise form of EBRT used to treat metastatic cervical cancer with high doses over few sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;SBRT is a highly precise form of radiation used to treat tumors in liver, lungs, or bones with few treatment sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;A precise form of radiation therapy used for treating small metastases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560605</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Palliative Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Palliative Radiation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of radiation therapy aimed at relieving symptoms and limiting tumor size.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Progression">
      <data key="d0">Progression</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The worsening or spread of cancer during or after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NCCN Guidelines">
      <data key="d0">NCCN Guidelines</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The NCCN Guidelines for Patients are informational resources to assist patients in understanding cancer care.&lt;SEP&gt;NCCN Guidelines provide detailed information on breast cancer diagnosis, treatment, and management.&lt;SEP&gt;The NCCN Guidelines for Patients provide information on managing nausea, vomiting, and other side effects of cancer treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;The NCCN Guidelines provide recommendations on cancer treatment, including fertility preservation options.&lt;SEP&gt;Guidelines provided by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network for patients on topics like fertility and family planning related to cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Guidelines published by the NCCN providing information on immunotherapy side effects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Treatment Options">
      <data key="d0">Treatment Options</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Available methods for managing cancer, including standard treatments and clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment options refer to the various therapies available for treating cancer, categorized by evidence level and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Various possible treatments for cancer, which information about biopsy results can influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Available methods for managing or curing cancer, including standard treatments and clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Myths">
      <data key="d0">Myths</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Misconceptions about clinical trials that can influence patient decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Advantages of participating in clinical trials, such as access to new treatments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Risks">
      <data key="d0">Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Potential negative outcomes or side effects associated with clinical trial participation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="U.S. Food and Drug Administration">
      <data key="d0">U.S. Food and Drug Administration</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The FDA approves drugs, devices, or treatments deemed safe and effective after clinical testing.&lt;SEP&gt;The FDA is responsible for approving drugs and treatments that prove safe and effective in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;The FDA is responsible for approving new drugs, devices, or treatments after successful clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560606</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thom">
      <data key="d0">Thom</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Thom is an individual who is a survivor of anal cancer and emphasizes the importance of advocacy and monitoring during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Avengers">
      <data key="d0">The Avengers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Incorrectly extracted, not relevant; omitted for correction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Study Sponsor">
      <data key="d0">Study Sponsor</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The sponsor is responsible for funding and managing research-related costs in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;The study sponsor funds research-related costs, including the study drug, and oversees the conduct of the clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NCCN Cancer Centers">
      <data key="d0">NCCN Cancer Centers</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">NCCN Cancer Centers are specialized cancer treatment and research centers accessible in the United States.&lt;SEP&gt;The NCCN Cancer Centers are designated by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network to provide specialized cancer treatment and support cancer research.&lt;SEP&gt;NCCN Cancer Centers are specialized facilities listed online for finding clinical trials in the U.S.&lt;SEP&gt;NCCN Cancer Centers are recognized institutions in the United States that provide specialized cancer treatment and participate in clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="National Cancer Institute">
      <data key="d0">National Cancer Institute</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. federal agency that provides information about cancer and clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;The NCI is a U.S. governmental agency that conducts and supports cancer research, including clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;The NCI is a U.S. federal agency supporting cancer research and providing information about clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Cancer Institute is a U.S. government agency dedicated to cancer research and clinical trial authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;U.S. government agency providing research, resources, and information related to cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="U.S. National Library of Medicine">
      <data key="d0">U.S. National Library of Medicine</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The U.S. National Library of Medicine maintains clinicaltrials.gov, a database of ongoing and completed clinical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;A federally funded medical library offering extensive medical research and clinical trial information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NCIs Cancer Information Service">
      <data key="d0">NCIs Cancer Information Service</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">NCI’s Cancer Information Service offers assistance in finding clinical trials and provides cancer-related information.&lt;SEP&gt;NCI’s Cancer Information Service provides assistance in finding clinical trials and information about cancer treatments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IMRT">
      <data key="d0">IMRT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy is an advanced radiation technique that limits exposure to surrounding tissues during anal cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ablative Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Ablative Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Ablative surgery, such as Abdominoperineal Resection (APR), involves removing the anus and creating a permanent colostomy for advanced or recurrent anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Survivorship">
      <data key="d0">Survivorship</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Survivorship encompasses physical, emotional, and financial issues faced by cancer survivors post-treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-treatment phase focusing on ongoing health, monitoring, and support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary Care Doctor">
      <data key="d0">Primary Care Doctor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The primary care doctor (GP or PCP) plays a crucial role in post-treatment follow-up and survivorship care planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bowel Function">
      <data key="d0">Bowel Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bowel function refers to the control and regularity of bowel movements, often affected after anal cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urinary Function">
      <data key="d0">Urinary Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Urinary function involves control over bladder activity, which may be impaired after radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sexual Function">
      <data key="d0">Sexual Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sexual function can be affected by anal cancer treatment, leading to changes in sexual health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radiation">
      <data key="d0">Radiation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiation is energy used in certain imaging tests like X-rays, but not in MRI.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation treatments use high-energy X-rays, gamma rays, or protons to destroy cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;High-energy radiation used in cancer treatment, including x-rays, gamma rays, and protons.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy uses high-energy rays to target cancer cells, with techniques like IMRT reducing exposure to healthy tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Follow-up Exam">
      <data key="d0">Follow-up Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Follow-up exams, including Digital Rectal Exam (DRE), are scheduled 8 to 12 weeks post-treatment to assess outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560608</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Colostomy">
      <data key="d0">Colostomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An opening created on the abdomen’s surface to allow stool to exit the body when reconnection isn't feasible or temporarily delayed.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical procedure that creates an opening in the abdomen for stool to exit when reconnecting the colon is unsafe.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy involves creating a stoma from the remaining colon to the outside of the abdomen to divert fecal matter.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical opening created for stool exit, often necessary after APR surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Survivorship Care Plan">
      <data key="d0">Survivorship Care Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A survivorship care plan summarizes cancer treatment history, side effects, follow-up recommendations, and transition to primary care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Psyllium">
      <data key="d0">Psyllium</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Psyllium is a fiber supplement used to manage bowel problems such as diarrhea, urgency, and incontinence after anal cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Psyllium is a fiber supplement derived from plant husks, used to help slow and thicken stool in cases of fecal incontinence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fecal Incontinence">
      <data key="d0">Fecal Incontinence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fecal incontinence is a condition characterized by the inability to control bowel movements, leading to accidental stool passage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Metamucil">
      <data key="d0">Metamucil</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Metamucil is a brand of psyllium-based fiber supplement that may assist in managing bowel consistency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dietitian">
      <data key="d0">Dietitian</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A professional specializing in nutrition, helping patients choose appropriate foods and fluids.&lt;SEP&gt;A dietitian is a healthcare professional who specializes in providing nutritional guidance to cancer survivors and patients with bowel issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pelvic Floor">
      <data key="d0">Pelvic Floor</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The pelvic floor consists of muscles supporting pelvic organs, crucial for bowel and bladder control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pelvic Floor Physical Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Pelvic Floor Physical Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Pelvic floor physical therapy involves exercises and techniques to strengthen pelvic muscles, including Kegel exercises.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kegel Exercises">
      <data key="d0">Kegel Exercises</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Kegel exercises are at-home exercises to tighten and relax pelvic muscles to improve strength and control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Dilator">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Dilator</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A vaginal dilator is a device used to stretch or widen the vagina, helping prevent or treat vaginal stenosis caused by radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Stenosis">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Stenosis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Vaginal stenosis is a condition where the vagina becomes shortened and narrowed due to radiation, affecting comfort and sexual activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Dilator Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Dilator Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Vaginal dilator therapy involves regular use of vaginal dilators to maintain or improve vaginal width and length after radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sexual Health Therapist">
      <data key="d0">Sexual Health Therapist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A sexual health therapist is a healthcare professional who helps manage sexual side effects after cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mental Health">
      <data key="d0">Mental Health</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mental health refers to emotional and psychological well-being and can be impacted by cancer diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quality of Life">
      <data key="d0">Quality of Life</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality of life measures overall well-being and daily functioning, often lowered after cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;An evaluation of overall well-being including physical, psychological, and social functioning during and after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fatigue">
      <data key="d0">Fatigue</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A common side effect of radiation therapy characterized by tiredness.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatigue is a common feeling of tiredness experienced by cancer survivors following treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dyspnea">
      <data key="d0">Dyspnea</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dyspnea refers to difficulty breathing, often reported by cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560610</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Insomnia">
      <data key="d0">Insomnia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Insomnia is difficulty sleeping that can occur following cancer therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560610</data>
