    <node id="Anal Cancer Foundation">
      <data key="d0">Anal Cancer Foundation</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Anal Cancer Foundation is an organization that provides support programs for anal cancer patients and caregivers.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization focused on providing support, resources, and advocacy for individuals affected by anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The Anal Cancer Foundation is a non-profit organization dedicated to supporting patients and raising awareness about anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560610</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ostomy">
      <data key="d0">Ostomy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An ostomy is a surgical opening that diverts waste outside the body, often requiring support for active living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560610</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ostomy Support Group">
      <data key="d0">Ostomy Support Group</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An ostomy support group is a community or meeting for individuals with ostomies to share experiences and support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560610</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ostomy Nurse">
      <data key="d0">Ostomy Nurse</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An ostomy nurse is a health care provider specializing in ostomy care and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560610</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Physical Activity">
      <data key="d0">Physical Activity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical activity refers to exercise and movement, which should be discussed with a healthcare provider before high-intensity exercise post-ostomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Healthy Habits">
      <data key="d0">Healthy Habits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Healthy habits include regular screening, immunizations, maintaining a healthy weight, and exercise to improve overall health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Screening">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer screening involves tests for early detection of cancers such as breast, cervical, colorectal, or prostate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Pressure Screening">
      <data key="d0">Blood Pressure Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood pressure screening is a health check recommended for maintaining cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hepatitis C Screening">
      <data key="d0">Hepatitis C Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Hepatitis C screening tests for the presence of hepatitis C virus infection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunizations">
      <data key="d0">Immunizations</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunizations such as the flu shot help prevent infectious diseases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Body Weight">
      <data key="d0">Body Weight</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maintaining a healthy body weight contributes to reduced risk of health issues and improved quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Moderate Exercise">
      <data key="d0">Moderate Exercise</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Engaging in about 150 minutes of moderate-intensity exercise weekly is recommended for health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Healthy Diet">
      <data key="d0">Healthy Diet</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A healthy diet should include lots of plant-based foods to support general health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aspirin">
      <data key="d0">Aspirin</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Aspirin is a medication that may be taken daily to help prevent future cancers, under medical guidance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bone Density">
      <data key="d0">Bone Density</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Monitoring bone density is recommended for patients who have undergone pelvic radiation to assess fracture risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Shortening">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Shortening</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Vaginal shortening, or vaginal stenosis, is a side effect of radiation therapy causing narrowing and shortening of the vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Narrowing">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Narrowing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Vaginal narrowing, or stenosis, results from radiation therapy, affecting sexual activity and examinations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pelvic Floor Muscles">
      <data key="d0">Pelvic Floor Muscles</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The pelvic floor muscles support pelvic organs and are involved in bowel, bladder control, and sexual function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Dilator Kit">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Dilator Kit</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A vaginal dilator kit contains different sizes of devices used to prevent or treat vaginal stenosis after radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Osteoporosis">
      <data key="d0">Osteoporosis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bone weakening associated with estrogen deficiency from surgical menopause.&lt;SEP&gt;Osteoporosis is a condition involving weakened bones that can be caused or worsened by pelvic radiation treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560611</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Doctor">
      <data key="d0">Doctor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Doctors evaluate medical and family history, perform physical and skin exams, and recommend tests for diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who advises patients on health matters, including planning pregnancy and cancer treatment considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;The doctor is a healthcare professional overseeing diagnosis and treatment, and providing guidance on communication with support persons.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who performs digital rectal exams, collects health history, and discusses prostate health with patients.&lt;SEP&gt;A healthcare professional who plans the next steps of patient care based on imaging results and discusses the results with the patient.&lt;SEP&gt;The doctor is a healthcare professional involved in ordering and interpreting imaging tests for patient diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctors are medical professionals advising patients on exercise, diet, screening, and treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Survivorship Resources">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Survivorship Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Resources offering guidance for cancer survivors on topics such as mental health, fatigue, sexual health, and complementary therapies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Complementary and Alternative Therapies">
      <data key="d0">Complementary and Alternative Therapies</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Complementary therapies include acupuncture, herbal remedies, homeopathy, hypnosis, meditation, Reiki, yoga, and massage, aimed at improving comfort and well-being during and after cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Treatment Decision">
      <data key="d0">Treatment Decision</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Making cancer treatment choices involves patient-doctor discussions, weighing risks and benefits, and considering personal values and quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Second Opinion">
      <data key="d0">Second Opinion</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Obtaining a second opinion involves consulting another doctor to review test results and treatment options before starting therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Requesting evaluations from other medical professionals for confirmation or alternative perspectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Support Groups">
      <data key="d0">Support Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Support groups are patient communities providing emotional assistance, shared experiences, and information for cancer patients at various treatment stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Organizations or networks providing emotional and social support to cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Test and Staging">
      <data key="d0">Test and Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Tests such as biopsy, high-resolution anoscopy, and genetic testing are used to diagnose, determine cancer stage and grade, and plan treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Tests">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic tests identify genes linked to hereditary conditions that increase the risk of pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic testing identifies inherited mutations related to pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are used to identify inherited mutations associated with increased risk of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests analyze DNA to detect mutations associated with cancer risk or progression.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are used to identify hereditary mutations that may influence cancer diagnosis, prognosis, or treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560612</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
