      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Questions to Ask">
      <data key="d0">Questions to Ask</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A list of important questions provided at the end of each chapter to help patients understand their care.&lt;SEP&gt;A section in the NCCN guidelines providing suggested questions to help patients understand their care better.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560616</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Lung Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lung cancer is a disease characterized by malignant growth in lung tissue, including the non-small cell type.&lt;SEP&gt;A malignant disease characterized by the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells in the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Lung cancer is a disease characterized by uncontrolled growth of cancer cells in the lungs, including NSCLC.&lt;SEP&gt;A malignancy of the lungs, with risk increased by smoking or vaping.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lung Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Lung Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lung carcinomas are cancers originating from the cells lining the airways, primarily forming from epithelial cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Cell Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Small Cell Lung Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A fast-growing, neuroendocrine lung cancer subtype.&lt;SEP&gt;Small cell lung cancer is a different type of lung cancer not covered under NSCLC and has distinct characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-dividing cancer originating from neuroendocrine cells, appearing small and oval or oat-shaped under a microscope, and representing the second most common lung cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neuroendocrine Tumors">
      <data key="d0">Neuroendocrine Tumors</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Neuroendocrine tumors are another form of lung carcinoma different from NSCLC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bronchioli">
      <data key="d0">Bronchioli</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Bronchioli are small airways inside the lungs that are extensions of the bronchi, ending in alveoli.&lt;SEP&gt;Bronchioli are smaller airways within the lungs branching from the bronchi.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lung Cells">
      <data key="d0">Lung Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Lung cells include those lining the airways and involved in the development of NSCLC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Abnormality">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Abnormality</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic abnormality such as the BCR::ABL gene fusion causes CML by promoting uncontrolled blood cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Involves the exchange of chromosome parts between chromosomes 9 and 22, creating the Philadelphia chromosome.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gene Fusion">
      <data key="d0">Gene Fusion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Gene fusion occurs when parts of two chromosomes combine abnormally, such as BCR::ABL resulting from chromosome exchange.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560617</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Abnormal Chromosome">
      <data key="d0">Abnormal Chromosome</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An abnormal chromosome, such as the Philadelphia chromosome, results from chromosome exchange and is associated with CML.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560618</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Test">
      <data key="d0">Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing for basal cell skin cancer involves biopsy, imaging, and medical history assessments to diagnose accurately.&lt;SEP&gt;Includes blood tests, genetic tests, and biopsies used for diagnosis and treatment planning in CML.&lt;SEP&gt;Includes blood tests, imaging studies, endoscopy, biopsy, biomarker testing, genetic risk testing, and performance status assessments used for diagnosis and treatment planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Tests such as hormone receptor testing and HER2 testing are performed on biopsy samples to determine cancer characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;A test is a procedure used to gather information about bone cancer, including imaging, blood tests, and biopsies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
