    <node id="MLH1">
      <data key="d0">MLH1</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">MLH1 is a gene involved in DNA mismatch repair, with mutations associated with cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;MLH1 is involved in DNA mismatch repair; mutations are related to colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MSH2">
      <data key="d0">MSH2</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">MSH2 is a gene linked to DNA repair, where mutations can lead to higher risk of cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;MSH2 gene mutations are associated with increased risk of colorectal and uterine cancers, as well as prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MSH6">
      <data key="d0">MSH6</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">MSH6 is a gene involved in DNA mismatch repair, with mutations potentially increasing cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;MSH6 mutation carriers have elevated risk for colorectal and uterine cancers alongside prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PALB2">
      <data key="d0">PALB2</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">PALB2 is a gene associated with increased risk for breast and prostate cancers upon mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;PALB2 is a gene associated with breast, ovarian, and pancreatic cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PMS2">
      <data key="d0">PMS2</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">PMS2 is a gene involved in DNA mismatch repair, linked to cancer susceptibility when mutated.&lt;SEP&gt;PMS2 mutations relate to increased risk of colorectal, uterine, and other cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Core">
      <data key="d0">Core</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A core is a small tissue sample from the prostate, approximately 1 to 20 millimeters long, used in biopsy testing for cancer detection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Germline">
      <data key="d0">Germline</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Germline mutations are inherited genetic changes that occur in every cell of the body and can increase the risk of various cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Germline Testing">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Germline Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic germline testing involves analyzing blood, urine, or saliva samples to detect characteristic gene mutations linked to cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PSA">
      <data key="d0">PSA</data>
      <data key="d1">biomarker</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate-specific antigen (PSA) levels in the blood can indicate prostate cancer presence or risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Molecular Biomarker Tests">
      <data key="d0">Molecular Biomarker Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Tests analyzing genetic or molecular features of tumors to assess risk and guide treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Groups">
      <data key="d0">Risk Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk groups classify prostate cancer into categories (very low to very high risk) based on clinical and molecular data.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk groups classify the level of cancer aggressiveness based on various assessments, affecting treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parallel">
      <data key="d0">Parallel</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parallel refers to assessing various factors such as risk groups, life expectancy, and biomarker tests to determine management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
