    <node id="Gleason Patterns">
      <data key="d0">Gleason Patterns</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Gleason patterns are microscopic patterns of prostate cancer cells used to evaluate cancer aggressiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560672</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gleason Score">
      <data key="d0">Gleason Score</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Gleason score is a numerical value assigned to prostate cancer based on biopsy patterns, indicating the cancer’s aggressiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gleason score is a numerical value derived from the two most common Gleason patterns in a biopsy, indicating cancer aggressiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Gleason score is a measurement used to evaluate prostate cancer aggressiveness, mentioned as part of additional assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560672</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Grade Group">
      <data key="d0">Grade Group</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Grade Group system classifies prostate cancer severity based on Gleason scores, ranging from Grade Group 1 (lowest) to Grade Group 5 (highest).&lt;SEP&gt;Grade Group is a classification system that organizes Gleason scores into five categories indicating cancer severity.&lt;SEP&gt;Grade Group is another assessment metric for prostate cancer, associated with risk stratification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560672</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Enlarged Prostate">
      <data key="d0">Enlarged Prostate</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">An enlarged prostate produces more PSA and may be related to conditions like benign prostatic hyperplasia.</data>
