    <node id="Invasive Breast Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Invasive Breast Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Invasive breast cancer is a type of cancer characterized by its growth beyond the ducts or lobules into surrounding tissue, with potential to spread through lymph or blood to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Invasive breast cancer is a form of breast cancer that spreads from ducts or lobules into surrounding breast tissue and possibly to lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Invasive breast cancer has spread outside the ducts or lobules into surrounding breast tissue and possibly to lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Invasive breast cancer has spread beyond the ducts or lobules into surrounding tissue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Breast">
      <data key="d0">Breast</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The breast is an organ and gland located on the chest, composed of milk ducts, lobules, fat, nerves, blood vessels, lymph vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue, involved in milk production and support.&lt;SEP&gt;The breast is an organ on the chest composed of milk ducts, lobules, fat, nerves, blood vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Breasts contain lobules, ducts, fat, blood and lymph vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue, and are the site of breast cancer development.&lt;SEP&gt;An organ and gland located on the chest composed of milk ducts, fat, nerves, blood vessels, lymph vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue, involved in milk production and delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The breast is an organ and gland on the chest composed of milk ducts, fat, nerves, vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;An organ consisting of lobules, ducts, fat, blood and lymph vessels, ligaments, connective tissue, and skin.&lt;SEP&gt;The breast is a tissue where cancer can develop, and it is a key area for biopsy and imaging procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lobules">
      <data key="d0">Lobules</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lobules are small structures within the breast that produce milk.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiny clusters of glands in the breast that produce milk.&lt;SEP&gt;Lobules are tiny clusters of glands in the breast that produce milk.&lt;SEP&gt;Lobules are the glandular structures in the breast that produce breast milk.&lt;SEP&gt;Structures within the breast that produce milk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Milk Ducts">
      <data key="d0">Milk Ducts</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Milk ducts connect lobules to the nipple, carrying milk to be expressed.&lt;SEP&gt;Thin tubes connecting lobules to the nipple, carrying milk in the breast.&lt;SEP&gt;Milk ducts connect lobules to the nipple, carrying breast milk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nipple">
      <data key="d0">Nipple</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The nipple is the raised part at the center of the areola on the breast.&lt;SEP&gt;The raised tip within the areola of the breast, part of the nipple-areola complex involved in milk delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The nipple is the raised tip within the areola allowing milk release.&lt;SEP&gt;The raised tip within the areola through which milk is delivered.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Areola">
      <data key="d0">Areola</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The areola is the darker pigmented ring surrounding the nipple on the breast.&lt;SEP&gt;The ring of darker skin around the nipple.&lt;SEP&gt;The areola is the darker skin ring surrounding the nipple.&lt;SEP&gt;Darker skin ring surrounding the nipple.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Secondary Tumors">
      <data key="d0">Secondary Tumors</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Secondary tumors are new growths formed when migrated cancer cells establish new tumors at distant sites.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mammary Glands">
      <data key="d0">Mammary Glands</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Mammary glands in the breast include lobules and ducts responsible for milk production and delivery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Epithelial Cells">
      <data key="d0">Epithelial Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Epithelial cells line the ducts and lobules of the breast and are the origin of most breast carcinomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560683</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ductal Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Ductal Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ductal carcinoma is a subtype of invasive breast cancer originating in the milk ducts, the most common type of breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Ductal carcinoma starts in the cells lining the milk ducts and is the most common type of breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Type of breast carcinoma starting in milk duct lining.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560683</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lobular Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Lobular Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lobular carcinoma is a subtype of invasive breast cancer arising in the milk-producing lobules of the breast.&lt;SEP&gt;Lobular carcinoma begins in the lobules of the breast.&lt;SEP&gt;Type of breast carcinoma starting in the lobules.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560683</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Axillary Lymph Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Axillary Lymph Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Axillary lymph nodes are located in the armpit and can be involved in breast cancer metastasis; their status influences cancer staging.&lt;SEP&gt;Axillary lymph nodes are lymph nodes located in the armpit area that drain lymph from the breast tissue and are involved in metastasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Axillary lymph nodes are located near the armpit and are involved in draining lymph from the breast.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph nodes located near the armpit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764560683</data>
      <data key="d6" />
