    <edge source="Diagnosis" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d7">9.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation "Biopsy" (Diagnosis) pertains to the medical procedure of obtaining tissue samples for diagnostic purposes across various conditions. Biopsies are routinely performed to confirm diagnoses of cancer and to guide subsequent treatment decisions. For example, biopsies are essential in diagnosing esophageal cancer, mouth cancer, ovarian cancer (particularly during surgery), and primary central nervous system (CNS) lymphoma. In the case of primary CNS lymphoma, a biopsy provides a definitive diagnosis by analyzing tumor tissue, which is critical for confirming the presence of this specific cancer. 

Additionally, biopsies are conducted by removing tissue samples from specific sites such as the cervix, lymph nodes, or bone marrow, enabling histological examination to determine the nature of abnormal tissue, such as malignancy or dysplasia. For conditions like chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL), biopsies of lymph nodes or marrow are performed when blood tests do not yield conclusive results, thereby confirming the diagnosis. Furthermore, biopsies play a role in detecting the presence of anal cancer or dysplasia, helping to establish precise diagnoses essential for planning appropriate treatments. Overall, biopsies remain a vital diagnostic tool across numerous cancers and disorders, facilitating accurate disease identification and informing effective management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d9">Primary CNS Lymphoma,Procedure,cancer detection,confirmation,confirms,disease confirmation,initial diagnosis method,sample collection,tissue analysis,tissue sampling</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764560803</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
