    </edge>
    <edge source="Treatment" target="Recurrence">
      <data key="d7">3.0</data>
      <data key="d8">For platinum-resistant recurrence, use non-platinum chemotherapy or targeted therapies like mirvetuximab soravtansine-gynx.&lt;SEP&gt;For platinum-sensitive recurrence, platinum-based chemotherapy, often combined with targeted therapy or surgery, is used.&lt;SEP&gt;Even after successful treatment, bladder cancer often recurs, requiring ongoing follow-up.</data>
      <data key="d9">approach,long-term management,monitoring</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764560822</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Treatment" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d7">5.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Surgery is often used as the primary treatment to remove early and locally advanced NSCLC.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical procedures may be performed to diagnose, remove, or treat ovarian cancer, often involving tissue biopsies.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgery is the primary treatment for ovarian cancer, involving hysterectomy, BSO, or fertility-sparing procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Most cases of pancreatic cancer involve surgery as part of treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgery is a treatment option for some primary and metastatic bone or thyroid cancers.</data>
      <data key="d9">approach,cancer removal,initial intervention,intervention,primary,removal of tumor,staging,used for</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764560843</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Treatment" target="schedule">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Intravesical treatments such as BCG and chemotherapy follow scheduled regimens to minimize side effects and maximize efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d9">intravesical therapy</data>
