    <edge source="Cancer" target="Staging">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Cancer staging is a systematic process used to assess the extent and severity of cancer within the body. It involves evaluating key factors such as tumor size, the extent of spread within the primary site, involvement of lymph nodes, and metastasis to distant organs. By analyzing these metrics, cancer staging provides a detailed picture of how far the disease has progressed, which is essential for informing treatment decisions and predicting patient prognosis.

Different cancers are staged using specific systems; for example, the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging system is commonly used to determine the stage of various cancers based on standardized criteria. In particular, staging plays a crucial role in cancers like ovarian and colon cancer, where assessing the spread within the ovaries or colon, and to adjacent lymph nodes or other organs, guides choices such as surgical intervention, chemotherapy, or other therapies. The overall goal of cancer staging is to delineate the disease's extent clearly, enabling clinicians to tailor treatment plans and provide accurate prognostic information to patients.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,describes,determines,extent,guidance,prognosis,progression,reflects,treatment planning,uses</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764560838</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cancer" target="Grading">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Cancer grading evaluates how aggressive the cancer cells are and their rate of growth.</data>
      <data key="d9">aggressiveness,growth rate</data>
