    <edge source="Cancer" target="Stage">
      <data key="d7">5.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Cancer stage reflects disease extent and informs prognosis and treatment plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer stages describe the extent and severity of disease based on TNM scores.&lt;SEP&gt;The stage of cancer (I, II, or III) is determined after surgical examination to guide further treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The stage of cancer is determined based on invasion depth and lymph node involvement, influencing treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer stage classification is based on TNM scores, ranging from stage 0 to stage IV.</data>
      <data key="d9">assessment,classification,prognosis,progression</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
