    <edge source="Blood" target="Blood Stem Cells">
      <data key="d7">5.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Blood stem cells in the bone marrow give rise to all blood cell types.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells within bone marrow develop into mature blood cells, a process disrupted in AML.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells originate in bone marrow and are involved in hematopoiesis, affected in AML.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells in bone marrow give rise to all blood cells through a process called differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells in bone marrow differentiate into various blood cell types.</data>
      <data key="d9">development,differentiate,differentiation,origin,source</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764560813</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood" target="Tumors">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Bladder tumors release blood into urine, causing hematuria which signals possible bladder cancer.</data>
