    <edge source="Blood" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d7">5.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Lymphocytes are a component of blood, involved in immune functions and affected in leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are blood cells involved in immune responses, including B cells, T cells, and NK cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are involved in immune responses including infection and tumor killing.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell critical to immune defense.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are specialized white blood cells that help fight infections and tumors.</data>
      <data key="d9">cell,cell type,component,immune defense,immune function,immune response,white blood cells</data>
