    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Lymphoid Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d7">4.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Blood stem cells differentiate into lymphoid progenitor cells, which develop into lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells give rise to lymphoid progenitor cells, which develop into lymphocytes affected by ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoid progenitor cells arise from blood stem cells and develop into lymphocytes that can be affected by ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells develop into lymphoid progenitor cells, which then produce lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d9">development,differentiation,origin</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764560913</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Blood Cell Formation">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Blood stem cells are the starting point for blood cell formation, including red cells, white cells, and platelets.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood stem cells give rise to all blood cells through blood cell formation.</data>
      <data key="d9">biological process,origin,process</data>
